hat's just above the SMA-20 ($80,894) and below the SMA-50 ($81,251), so the short-term trend leans bearish.\n- **Volatility is low.**\n\n**What this means for a trade:** RSI alone gives no signal here. It's mid-range, so there's no overbought or oversold edge. A trader would wait.\n\n## Cautions for beginners\n1. **Strong trends break the rule.** In a powerful uptrend, RSI can stay above 70 for a long time. \"Overbought\" doesn't mean \"about to drop.\"\n2. **Don't use it alone.** Pair it with trend indicators (SMA) and MACD. When several agree, confidence goes up.\n3. **Watch for divergence.** If price makes a new high but RSI doesn't, momentum is fading. That's an early warning.\n4. **Match it to your contract length.** RSI is most useful for short-term contracts (ticks to minutes).\n\nWant me to show what an actual overbought or oversold setup looks like on another market? I can also explain MACD next.\n\n*This is educational analysis, not financial advice. Binary options carry significant risk — you can lose your entire stake on any single trade.*"}]